## 2. What “proper sized for EcoSuit” does and does not mean

116 MW is vehicle-scale electrical / thermal power.
It is not wearable point-mass gravity.

A 1.75 billion tonne singularity in the torso is 132 g mean acceleration and ~176 g of tide across the chest. The crew is a smear on the pelvic yoke before the first plate latch cycles.

So the EcoSuit reference ABH is **not in the suit**.
It is a remote core for a stage the suit rides, parked metres-to-tens-of-metres away, on a boom or a separate hopper bus.

If you insist on “in the backpack” you are describing a 1.75 × 10⁹ t object whose near-field rips the hemp-ceramic stack off the frame. That is not MK.I hardware.

