## 3. Ice particulates at 2600 am

Two jobs people conflate. Only one is even paper-legal.

### 3.1 Accretion into the hole (stoke Mc²)
Horizon is still ~100,000 × smaller than a water molecule.
Capture area is still 1.4 × 10⁻²⁸ m².
You do not pour ice into 2.6 fm.

Unlike 1.3 am, Hawking is now *below* Eddington. Radiation will not automatically blow the feed away. That does not create a funnel. Ice still has to become a plasma disk at nuclear scales and lose angular momentum. There is no plumbing for that on a suit. Label it “not a feed line.”

### 3.2 Ice as working fluid around the hole (the only honest use)
Leave M alone. Steal heat. Ice is reaction mass / coolant for a heat engine sitting at a controlled standoff.

- 116 MW intercepted at ~3 m is a 1 MW/m² class exchanger if you build a ~10 m² catcher — brutal, but a number engineers recognize.
- 116 MW at ~100 m is solar-constant-ish on a large shield.
- Directed jet, 100% of P into ve = 4.4 km/s: T = 2P/ve ≈ **53 kN**.
- 1% conversion: **0.53 kN**. 0.01%: **5 N**.

53 kN lifts ~5.4 t against Earth g. That is a small hopper / abort pack, **not** the 85–100 kN Earth-liftoff class of a 6.7 t hydrolox Moon stack, and not 15 km/s of Δv.

Energy in the hole would cover Earth→Moon 10¹⁸ times over.
Power and thrust available to a nozzle would not.

Hawking still has no throttle. P_H is fixed by M. Feed (if you could) makes it dimmer. Starve it and it barely changes on human timescales — lifetime is 10¹³ years.

