## 5. EcoSuit integration rules (2600 am reference)

1. Core is never inside the pressure garment or the plate stack.
2. Minimum crewed standoff is set by g and tide, not by Hawking: keep the hole **tens of metres** off the body on a boom / hopper bus. At 10 m, g ≈ 0.12 g and flux ≈ 92 kW/m² — still a shield problem, no longer a tide problem.
3. Ice tanks live on that bus. No feed line claims to terminate at Rs.
4. Heat catcher and nozzle live on the bus. Plume never kisses hemp cores.
5. Suit-side: SEAs in hold during a burn, V-EBMs lock plates, DEAs off, ceramic is TPS/MMOD only.
6. HV inhibit, vacuum interlocks, and Case A launch loads do not change.
7. Label every drawing “ABH-2600, remote, not worn.”

