## Ice particulates
Accretion into the hole: no. Horizon is 200 million times smaller than a water molecule. Hawking wind is 70,000× Eddington. Ice never reaches Rs.

Ice as working fluid around the hole: only as reaction mass in a remote heat engine. That engine sits kilometres away. It is a stage, not a sternum core. 0.1% intercept of 465 TW is still 465 GW.

Hawking power is fixed by mass (P ∝ 1/M²). Feed it (if you could) and it dims. Starve it and it heats up. No throttle.

## Earth→Moon
Energy: yes, by 15 orders of magnitude.
Thrust, throttle, standoff, crew survival, manufacture: no.
Making the object is concentrating ~1e5 years of world energy into 1.3 am. Not a line on the EcoSuit traveler.

